### 5.2 Silver Tasks

> **Note on the "DQ Check" column.** The cell text combines two independent
> gates that the per-table YAML config keeps separate. Read the cell as the
> union of:
>
> - `empty_input_behavior` (one of `fail` / `write_empty`) — what to do
>   when the upstream source is empty for `ds`. Evaluated BEFORE any
>   transformation runs.
> - `se_action_if_failed` (one of `fail` / `drop` / `ignore`) — how SE
>   responds to row_dq/agg_dq violations. Evaluated AFTER transformation,
>   BEFORE write. Per-rule `action_if_failed` declarations take
>   precedence over this fail-closed default.
>
> Critical tables (patients, encounters, allergies, FK dimensions) set
> `empty_input_behavior: fail` AND `se_action_if_failed: fail`. Non-critical
> clinical tables typically use `empty_input_behavior: write_empty` AND
> `se_action_if_failed: drop` (route rejected rows to quarantine, write
> the rest).

